💭 A fresh object of a class that is declared further down, handed straight to a method
💭 that only borrows it.
💭
💭 Expected: the program prints 7.
💭 What happens: the compiler aborts with
💭   MFFlowCategory::isEscaping(): Assertion `!isUnknown()' failed.
💭 ASTInitialization::analyseMemoryFlow asks whether the initializer keeps its object
💭 before the initializer has been analysed. A compiler built without assertions would
💭 read "unknown" as "does not escape" and put the object on the stack.
💭
💭 Binding the object to a variable first is fine: 🆕📦 7❗️ ➡️ box, then 🔢 box❗️.
